cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Lazarus AP: an emulator of the IBM AP-101S Space Shuttle flight computer"
message: >-
  If you use this work, please cite it, and please also cite the
  recovered artifacts it stands on (see references below).
type: software
abstract: >-
  A cited, test-driven emulation of the IBM AP-101S general-purpose
  computer that flew every Space Shuttle mission, together with the
  recovered flight toolchain. Runs the genuine HAL/S flight runtime
  library and programs built by the original Space Shuttle compiler.
  Instruction-set details unsupported by primary sources are marked
  UNVERIFIED and left unimplemented rather than reconstructed.
keywords:
  - Space Shuttle
  - AP-101S
  - emulator
  - HAL/S
  - history of computing
  - retrocomputing
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/USER/lazarus-ap"
references:
  - type: report
    title: >-
      Space Shuttle Model AP-101S Principles of Operation with Shuttle
      Instruction Set
    number: 85-C67-001
    authors:
      - name: IBM Federal Systems Division
    url: "https://www.ibiblio.org/apollo/Shuttle/Shuttle%20GPC%20Software%20Model%20AP-101S.pdf"
    notes: The primary source for the instruction set.
  - type: software
    title: Virtual AGC
    authors:
      - family-names: Burkey
        given-names: Ronald
    url: "https://www.ibiblio.org/apollo/"
    notes: >-
      Source of the recovered HAL/S-FC compiler, the ASM101S assembler,
      the flight runtime library, the fixture programs, and the yaGPC2
      cross-check emulator. This project would not exist without it.
